title the template was repaired and the launcher was left, so the loop-prompt surface gets a guard
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think The cold roster read 74 guards, 73 green, in 30 minutes. The single red is declared_ceiling, which is REDS %295, Mind's, and gated -- the same reading the previous lap took, so no new tree red opened and the standfast pointed at the ledger's own open rows.
think Six rows stand open. %230, %291, %295 and %301's five folds are gated or each want their own lap; %304's remainder is constel/, which is Dream's lane on this pier; %306's redraw is Pond's. %307 was the one open clause an agent on this bench can close: "no guard reads an instruction file against the gate list."
think Before writing that guard I measured what it would read, since a guard written against a remembered surface measures a remembered surface. An inline awk over the loop-prompt rooms -- recursion-prompts/*.md and tools/l/launch-* -- split each line into clauses at "; " and ". ", looked for three gated command tokens, and asked whether a refusal word stood in the same clause. It named two BARE lines, and both were in tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish.
think That is REDS %307's own root arriving a second time. The previous lap repaired recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md, which is the TEMPLATE a future prompt is written from. tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish lines 66 and 86 print the seat prompts a hand actually pastes to START a loop, and both still said "every fifth round ... also project and force-push the public seed with bash ~/grain/publish-seed.sh". The three launchers written since the role swap -- dream, hush, silence -- each already say "never run publish-seed.sh". Only the elder one drifted, and it is the one that reaches a machine.
think Both lines were repaired with a sed through the original inode (cat tmp > file), so the exec bit the repository tracks survived -- .claude/rules/exec-bit.md. The replacement carries no apostrophe, because the text sits inside a single-quoted shell string that loop_prompt_parse exists to protect.
think The guard's precision problem is that these same files must be free to NAME the gated command in order to forbid it. The rule that answers it is form rather than sentiment: a gated command token must stand in a clause carrying a refusal word. Proven on the real tree before it was written down -- two BARE, five FREE, no false positive on any of the five correct mentions.
obs The roster is discovered from git ls-files rather than typed, which is REDS %277's lesson borrowed: a roster typed by hand grows when somebody remembers, and this whole row exists because nobody did. It reads 27 files today and will read the 28th on the lap it arrives.
obs The scan reads launchers as SOURCE and never runs them. loop_prompt_parse runs the four printers to measure their printout; running launch-claude.rish would start an agent. Reading the string is enough here, since the string is what ships.
obs The control plants the real pre-repair sentence verbatim rather than an invented one, so the refusal is proven against the fault that actually happened. Eleven cases: the bare line bitten and its token named, the repair freed, both other tokens bitten, prose about force-pushing left free, an absent file told apart from a passing one -- and the precision case, where a "never" two clauses away is refused the power to launder a bare instruction.
obs Named rather than left to be found: four of the seven custody gates name an ACT rather than a command -- provisioning, moving funds, a real Kumara seed, a collaborator's domain -- and no grep reaches those. Clause proximity is a reading rather than a comprehension. Word presence is the check; a reader is the standard.
obs The ledger pin had five bytes of room, so the recital's own rule freed it: the pin keeps the three most recent pointer lines and sixteen stood. Twelve folded to construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md with their link targets re-anchored to bare basenames; all twelve resolve. The autoproject96 standfast note stayed flat, because it still stands rather than pointing at a closed fold.
obs The roster's own header carried the same cut cadence in prose -- "the fifth round, where the council rota closes its cycle and the seed ships". Corrected in the same pass, since a comment that teaches a cut cadence teaches it to whoever reads the roster next.
obs The rota read row 4, Earth/Mercury, the concrete, sense of smell: the one-clock naming law cardinal, Two Rooms fixed, the marked value dual. The fixed seat governed the lap -- a room is smelled at the door, from its own status line, before a body paragraph is trusted -- and that is exactly what measuring the surface before writing the guard turned out to be.
